  "scope": "Executed C17 scheduling, cache, HTTP and native CLI/report contracts with synthetic model frontiers. NOT-INFERENCE; no original-weight GPU numerical, quality or performance qualification.",
  "implementation": [
    "Separate schedule ABI 1 and submit factory copy 1..64 ascending physical position/scale steps before publication. Request ABI 8, existing core option/info and live-job ABI layouts are unchanged.",
    "One existing inference owner splits prefill and caps each row AR/MTP advance. A due last-prefill/first-decode row waits for its change; actual retained position and effective scales are confirmed.",
    "Position zero applies before scoped cache lookup; token-key restore is bounded by the next step. Compatible shorter prefixes remain usable; mixed-history captures preserve image identity.",
    "Native core --dir-steering-plan records canonical binary32 plan, applied positions, statuses and final scope/history. Reports reject unfulfilled/crossed steps, excessive cache reuse and different plan identities.",
    "LIE extension GET/POST /v1/responses/{id}/steering and /v1/chat/completions/{id}/steering projects asynchronous tickets and confirmed policy for retained single-choice requests; no provider call or wait on the libuv thread.",
    "No inference thread, product/default-test Python dependency, numerical-provider edit or DS4 tensor/framing change."
  ],
  "coverage": [
    "Executed aligned and DS4-KVC AR/MTP/vision/joint lifetimes and real RAM/SSD codecs; cache reuse cannot skip an intermediate change.",
    "Copied caller inputs, malformed/duplicate JSON, no-op initial changes, full 64-step admission, out-of-generation refusal, unreached EOS/cancellation, pure refusal and model-poison failure.",
    "One scheduled and one uniform peer share native dispatch with independent burst limits and histories; native C2 cohorts repeat complete plan identities and output IDs.",
    "Both HTTP APIs admit a change during an owned slow-prefill fixture, reject malformed scales and retirement, and project owner confirmation; tests own private ephemeral loopback ports.",
    "21 final Debug and 21 final ASan/UBSan/LeakSanitizer CTest checks, 3 build-off checks and 32 C++ public headers pass. Test children use a PATH without Python; GPUs masked. Host fixtures only."
  ],
